-- title:
--   No nonzero locally nilpotent derivation of $\mathrm{SL}_2\times\mathbb{A}^1$ of Euler weight $e\le 0$ kills $a$, $d$ and $u$
-- statement:
--   Let $T=\mathbb{C}[a,b,c,d,u]/(ac-bd-1)$ be the coordinate ring of $\mathrm{SL}_2\times\mathbb{A}^1$: the classes of $a,b,c,d$ are the entries of the matrix $\begin{pmatrix}a&b\\ d&c\end{pmatrix}$ of determinant $1$, and $u$ is a free coordinate; $T$ is an integral domain. Let $\delta$ and $\eta$ be the $\mathbb{C}$-derivations of $T$ determined by
--
--   $$
--   \delta(a)=\delta(d)=\delta(u)=0,\quad \delta(b)=a,\quad \delta(c)=d;\qquad \eta(b)=\eta(c)=\eta(u)=0,\quad \eta(a)=b,\quad \eta(d)=c,
--   $$
--
--   and let $\theta=[\delta,\eta]=\delta\eta-\eta\delta$ be the Euler derivation, so that $\theta(a)=a$, $\theta(d)=d$, $\theta(b)=-b$, $\theta(c)=-c$ and $\theta(u)=0$. (Geometrically, $\delta$, $\eta$ and $\theta$ generate right multiplication on $\mathrm{SL}_2$ by the upper unipotent, lower unipotent and diagonal subgroups.)
--
--   **Theorem.** Let $E$ be a $\mathbb{C}$-derivation of $T$ and let $e\in\mathbb{Z}$ with $e\le0$. Assume that $E\neq0$, that $E$ is locally nilpotent (every $r\in T$ satisfies $E^n(r)=0$ for some $n\in\mathbb{N}$), that $E$ shifts Euler weights by $e$, and that $E$ kills $a$, $d$ and $u$:
--
--   $$
--   \theta\bigl(E(r)\bigr)-E\bigl(\theta(r)\bigr)=e\,E(r)\ \text{ for all } r\in T,\qquad E(a)=E(d)=E(u)=0 .
--   $$
--
--   Then these assumptions are contradictory. Equivalently, every locally nilpotent derivation $E$ of $T$ that satisfies the displayed conditions for some integer $e\le0$ is zero.
--
--   The condition $[\theta,E]=eE$ says that $E$ is homogeneous of degree $e$ for the torus action generated by $\theta$. The statement is the last step of a rigidity theorem for $T$: there, a homogeneous locally nilpotent derivation is first shown to kill $a$, $d$ and $u$, and this result then forces it to vanish.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $T$ is `MvPolynomial (Fin 5) ℂ ⧸ (X 0 * X 3 - X 2 * X 1 - 1)`, and $a,d,b,c,u$ are the classes of `X 0, …, X 4` in this order. The Euler derivation is `Euler = ⁅δ, η⁆`, the weight condition is `FiberShift E e`, local nilpotence is `LND.LocallyNilpotent E`, and the conclusion is `False`.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Algebra/AffineCancellation/DeterminantRigidity.lean#L83-L127

